# Project MCP (`.cursor/mcp.json`)

Use these MCP servers when they help the task:

- **context7** — Resolve library IDs and fetch up-to-date docs before implementing unfamiliar APIs or setup steps. Prefer Context7 over guessing version-specific behavior.
- **chrome-devtools** — Debug and inspect a real Chrome instance (console, network, performance). Prefer over Playwright when DevTools-level inspection is needed.
- **playwright** — Browser automation via accessibility snapshots (E2E flows, form filling, screenshots). Prefer for scripted navigation and repeatable UI checks.
- **engram** — Durable project memory across sessions. At session start, search/load relevant memories; after meaningful decisions or completed work, save concise memories.

Context7 optional API key: set user env var `CONTEXT7_API_KEY` (from context7.com/dashboard) for higher limits.

After editing `.cursor/mcp.json`, reload the Cursor window so MCP servers reconnect.
